  - language: 10
    solidName: Tetrahedron
    solidFamily: Platonic Solid
    description: The most fundamental three-dimensional shape consisting of four
      triangular faces that provide maximum structural rigidity.
    fact1: The only self-dual Platonic solid because its dual is another tetrahedron.
    fact2: Minimum number of faces needed to enclose a 3D volume.
    fact3: The strongest structural shape used in truss engineering.
